Adafruit TinyUSB Library 3.7.7 (the one arduino-pico 6.3.x bundles) as the RP2040 USB peer uses it.
tests/run_hardware.py applies this to the pinned release and puts the result in the peer's sketch.yaml
(libraries: - dir:), ahead of the bundled copy.

1. src/portable/raspberrypi/rp2040/ (hcd_rp2040.c, dcd_rp2040.c, rp2040_usb.c, rp2040_usb.h): replaced with
   hathach/tinyusb 38bd85a0c0 (2026-10-25). 3.7.7 took TinyUSB at dcd2a4bd (2026-05-11); the host driver fixed
   since then is what the tests ran into:
   - 72e09788e4: a control transfer's OUT data stage (SET_LINE_CODING, SET_REPORT) went out as DATA0, and a
     device that checks the toggle (CH32RVUsbDevice) dropped it and waited.
   - e204823875 (#4166), 3174e76034 (#4177): transfers left on EPX or an interrupt endpoint when a device
     goes away are aborted. Without them the next device's enumeration panics ("buf_ctrl ... already
     available") - CH32RVUsbDevice's end() + begin() was enough.
2. tusb_config_rp2040.h: tuh_edpt_xfer() on, for the classes the host has no driver for (vendor bulk,
   CCID, NCM); and the host's enumeration buffer 1024 bytes, not 256 (a configuration descriptor longer than
   it, as usb_contracts' 302, failed the enumeration at an assert).

